{"title":"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34831b9eadcb62e10bad479e226ccd953c0dc5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 + xy + 3y^2 - 11x - 20y + 40 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"291\" height=\"18\" /> is an ellipse in the first quadrant of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-plane. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the maximum and minimum values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f9d06b1ffe0694bd2be52b3bb95a8733098e367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac yx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> over all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> on the ellipse. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd5e63df32eca344900b89f4d5d561b67a98913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{10} \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac 72 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac 92 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 2\\sqrt{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"408\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2004_12B_AMC-21.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/36/2004_12B_AMC-21.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"203\" height=\"264\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f9d06b1ffe0694bd2be52b3bb95a8733098e367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac yx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> represents the slope of a line passing through the origin. It follows that since a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8cab3b86d4a13c3cc3680c32aaa80cc854689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> intersects the ellipse at either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f41feba960f5daf82e943291e40d85d0379a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, the minimum and maximum are given when the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8cab3b86d4a13c3cc3680c32aaa80cc854689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> is a tangent, with only one point of intersection. Substituting,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/7810f02a1d842903268ef4e400f6355a7262fa0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^2 + x(mx) + 3(mx)^2 - 11x - 20(mx) + 40 = 0\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"19\" />\nRearranging by the degree of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3db7670b17d2532db53dee1c1c5e8c1cc7a786c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(3m^2 + m + 2)x^2 - (20m + 11)x + 40 = 0\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"19\" />\nSince the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1fe0afdea68630af2bda225ce5f2978b5ba0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" /> is tangent to the ellipse, we want the discriminant, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b41331a8f9d71b05e9dae9769abf4b648dce70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(20m+11)^2 - 4\\cdot 40 \\cdot (3m^2 + m + 2) = -80m^2 + 280m - 199\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"20\" />\nto be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, which is the sum of the roots of the above quadratic. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%E2%80%99s_formulas&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Vieta’s formulas (page does not exist)\">Vieta’s formulas</a>, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f8ad526281a8417d9dcc3501a392d4d2b225701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{280}{80} = \\frac{7}{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B\">2004 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203502\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 201/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive pa